$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 CS2 {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Comsig"
  m_sTextData "<h2>CALLSIGNS</h2>"\
  "• Our team - Platan41"\
  ""\
  "<h2>PASSWORDS</h2>"\
  "All can be changed at CO's discretion."\
  "• <b>Challenge:</b> Yoke | <b>Password:</b> bloke"\
  "• Running password: 1"
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "GC_IRA"
  }
  m_iOrder 5
 }
 EF2 {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "Enemy forces consist of British Army elements operating throughout the marked area of operations. Their strength is estimated at approximately 40 personnel, consisting primarily of light infantry supported by a small number of mobile elements."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
  "• All British personnel are equipped with weapon optics."\
  "• The British hold an overall advantage in firepower, numbers, and mobility."\
  "• They are operating 4x WMIKs, each equipped with a roof-mounted .50 cal heavy machine gun and a forward-mounted GPMG, providing significant mobile firepower."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "GC_IRA"
  }
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 FF2 {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "We are the Irish Republican Army (IRA), Platan Cell. Our force consists of approximately 45 personnel distributed between our established positions along the MSR and throughout the surrounding terrain. Our team is staging at the most western barn yard."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
  "• We have two occupied machine gun positions: 1x M2 .50 cal and 1x PKM. Refer to maps for their locations."\
  "• Our sapper is equipped with explosive charges, with additional charges available in a small supply box at our staging area. He should use these to establish traps and exploit opportunities against the enemy where possible."\
  "• Our forces are lightly equipped but highly mobile, allowing us to conduct coordinated hit-and-run engagements before breaking contact and repositioning."\
  ""\
  "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>"\
  "At our staging area we have a motorbike, an unarmed UAZ, and one PKM armed UAZ which contains:"\
  "- 1x AT mine"\
  "- 1x Portable ladder"\
  "- 1x Handheld periscope"\
  "- 6x Red flares"\
  "- 4x PKM belts for the UAZ."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "GC_IRA"
  }
  m_iOrder 3
 }
 MIS2 {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Mission"
  m_sTextData "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
  "We are to conduct a <b>DELIBERATE DEFENCE</b> by <b>DELAYING & DISRUPTING</b> the advancing British forces in order to deny them control of the MSR."\
  ""\
  "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
  "Our recent ambushes have caused significant disruption along the route. In response, British forces are attempting to push us out of the area and seize our established ambush positions along the MSR."\
  ""\
  "The first two ambush locations are considered expendable and do not need to be defended at all costs. Their loss is acceptable if it allows us to preserve our strength for the final position."\
  ""\
  "The final ambush location must be held. Its loss would severely limit our ability to operate along the route and conduct further attacks. Delay the British advance, disrupt their movements, and prevent them from gaining control of the MSR."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "GC_IRA"
  }
  m_iOrder 4
 }
 SIT2 {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
  "DTL: 21/07/1991, 0600hrs, Northern Ireland."\
  "Weather: Clear, light winds, visibility 1km+, with forecast of change."\
  ""\
  "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
  "Operation Banner remains ongoing as British forces continue to support the Royal Ulster Constabulary in maintaining security and disrupting paramilitary activity across Northern Ireland."\
  ""\
  "Over recent months, IRA personnel have repeatedly used three isolated farmyards overlooking the Main Supply Route (MSR) between Lovetin and Kamoryn to conduct ambushes against British Army patrols, Royal Ulster Constabulary units, and, on occasion, civilian traffic. The locations are not permanently occupied, with personnel moving in and out using irregular patterns to avoid detection."\
  ""\
  "Following weeks of surveillance and intelligence gathering, C Company has been tasked with conducting a coordinated search operation to clear the suspected locations, deny the IRA use of the farmyards, and restore freedom of movement along the route."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "GC_IRA"
  }
  m_iOrder 1
 }
}